ey":"messages","value":"[\n    {\n      \"role\": \"system\",\n      \"content\": \"Summarize the following passage, which probably describes a conspiracy belief, in a single sentence. Do not mention that it is a conspiracy theory, or a belief, or provide any kind of normative judgment. Merely accurately describe the content of the conspiracy theory in a single sentence, framing it in a manner that suggests the conspiracy is TRUE. So, even if the writer is arguing that the earth is not flat, you would say 'the earth is flat'). Frame it as a true assertion (regardless of whether evidence actually supports the belief). If the statement is already short, no need to change it very much. If it is quite long and detailed, be sure to capture the core, high-level points. If the respondent equivocates or couches their language in uncertainty, be sure not to include this equivocation in your summary. Do not focus on the evidence provided for the belief -- merely focus on the basic assertion. That is, use the evidence and justifications they might provide only for context. For your information, the passage was written by a participant in an online academic survey in response to the following two questions: < Q1: ${q:\/\/QID67\/QuestionText} > < ${q:\/\/QID68\/QuestionText} > Again, your role is to summarize the overarching belief captured by this response. Your summary will be shown to the participant, who will be asked to rate their agreement with the statement; their belief in the summary will be used as a psychometrics-style item in a scientific experiment.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"user\",\n      \"content\": \"Question 1 Response: ${q:\/\/QID67\/ChoiceTextEntryValue}, Question 2 Response: ${q:\/\/QID68\/ChoiceTextEntryValue}\"\n    }\n  ]","parameterType":"JSON"},{"key":"max_tokens","value":"150","parameterType":"Number"}],"Body":{"model":"gpt-4o","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"Summarize the following passage, which probably describes a conspiracy belief, in a single sentence. Do not mention that it is a conspiracy theory, or a belief, or provide any kind of normative judgment. Merely accurately describe the content of the conspiracy theory in a single sentence, framing it in a manner that suggests the conspiracy is TRUE. So, even if the writer is arguing that the earth is not flat, you would say 'the earth is flat'). Frame it as a true assertion (regardless of whether evidence actually supports the belief). If the statement is already short, no need to change it very much. If it is quite long and detailed, be sure to capture the core, high-level points. If the respondent equivocates or couches their language in uncertainty, be sure not to include this equivocation in your summary. Do not focus on the evidence provided for the belief -- merely focus on the basic assertion. That is, use the evidence and justifications they might provide only for context. For your information, the passage was written by a participant in an online academic survey in response to the following two questions: < Q1: ${q:\/\/QID67\/QuestionText} > < ${q:\/\/QID68\/QuestionText} > Again, your role is to summarize the overarching belief captured by this response. Your summary will be shown to the participant, who will be asked to rate their agreement with the statement; their belief in the summary will be used as a psychometrics-style item in a scientific experiment."},{"role":"user","content":"Question 1 Response: ${q:\/\/QID67\/ChoiceTextEntryValue}, Question 2 Response: ${q:\/\/QID68\/ChoiceTextEntryValue}"}],"max_tokens":150},"ContentType":"application\/json","Headers":[{"key":"Authorization","value":"Bearer REDACTED_OPENAI_KEY_ROTATE_ME"}],"ResponseMap":[{"key":"choices.0.message.content","value":"conRestatement"}],"FireAndForget":false,"SchemaVersion":0,"StringifyValues":true},{"Type":"WebService","FlowID":"FL_213","URL":"https:\/\/api.openai.com\/v1\/chat\/completions","Method":"POST","RequestParams":[],"EditBodyParams":[{"key":"mode