tryValue}, Question 2 Response: ${q:\/\/QID70\/ChoiceTextEntryValue}\"\n  }\n]","parameterType":"JSON"},{"key":"max_tokens","value":"150","parameterType":"Number"}],"Body":{"model":"gpt-4o","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are classifying responses from participants in an online survey about conspiracy theories. Participants answered two questions:\n\n(Q1) Asked participants explicitly to briefly describe a conspiracy theory they feel genuinely uncertain about (they could see it either being true or false).\n(Q2) Asked participants to discuss specific reasons for their partial belief, explicitly mentioning both evidence for belief and skepticism.\n\nYour task is to determine whether the participant\u2019s responses reflect ambivalent or uncertain belief in a conspiracy theory or a closely related idea.\n\nUse the everyday (folk) concept of a conspiracy theory, not a strict academic definition. Borderline or loosely related scenarios, like cryptid sightings, paranormal phenomena, or secretive cover-ups, are acceptable and should be classified as TRUE if uncertainty or ambivalence is at least plausible.\n\nClassify as TRUE if:\n- The response clearly or implicitly indicates uncertainty or ambivalence about the described theory.\n- The participant describes a specific conspiracy theory (or something closely related) without explicitly stating their level of certainty. Given the original survey instructions explicitly requested a conspiracy theory they're unsure about, presume implicit ambivalence and classify as TRUE.\n\nClassify as FALSE only if:\n- The participant explicitly expresses firm belief or complete rejection of the conspiracy theory without any sign of uncertainty or ambivalence.\n\n Classify as INVALID only if \/n - The participant\u2019s responses are nonsensical, random, clearly inattentive, irrelevant, or obviously off-topic. \/n - Responses appear auto-generated, robotic, spam-like, include characters or script a human is unlikely to use, or otherwise clearly indicate lack of genuine engagement.\n\nWhen in doubt, or if ambivalence is unclear, default to classifying responses as TRUE, favoring false positives. Only respond with TRUE or FALSE or INVALID"},{"role":"user","content":"Question 1 Response: ${q:\/\/QID69\/ChoiceTextEntryValue}, Question 2 Response: ${q:\/\/QID70\/ChoiceTextEntryValue}"}],"max_tokens":150},"ContentType":"application\/json","Headers":[{"key":"Authorization","value":"Bearer REDACTED_OPENAI_KEY_ROTATE_ME"}],"ResponseMap":[{"key":"choices.0.message.content","value":"isEquivocal"}],"FireAndForget":false,"SchemaVersion":0,"StringifyValues":true},{"Type":"Branch","FlowID":"FL_283","Description":"New Branch","BranchLogic":{"0":{"0":{"LogicType":"EmbeddedField","LeftOperand":"isEquivocal","Operator":"EqualTo","RightOperand":"INVALID","_HiddenExpression":false,"Type":"Expression","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">isEquivocal<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Equal to<\/span> <span class=\"RightOpDesc\"> INVALID <\/span>"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Flow":[{"Type":"EndSurvey","FlowID":"FL_284","EndingType":"Advanced","Options":{"Advanced":"true","SurveyTermination":"Redirect","EOSRedirectURL":"https:\/\/samplicio.us\/s\/ClientCallBack.aspx?RIS=20&RID=${e:\/\/Field\/rid}"}}]}]}]}]}]},{"Type":"Standard","ID":"BL_ePNbZOXPITDPHCu","FlowID":"FL_252","Autofill":[]}]}]},{"Type":"EmbeddedData","FlowID":"FL_34","EmbeddedData":[{"Description":"userBeliefLevel","Type":"Custom","Field":"userBeliefLevel","VariableType":"String","DataVisibility":[],"AnalyzeText":false,"Value":"${q:\/\/QID66\/TotalSum}"},{"Description":"endorse_string","Type":"Custom","Field":"endorse_string","VariableType":"String","DataVisibility":[],"AnalyzeText":false,"Value":"\"believe\""},{"Description":"endorse_string2","Type":"Custom","Field":"endorse_string2","VariableType":"String","DataVisibility":[],"AnalyzeText":false,"Value":"\"this belief is supported\""}]},{"Type